Z||000000||cool85gt||10-26-2001||04:35 PM||||the other day i was driving in my 85 GT when i killed it at an intersection. when i went to go restart it would turn over but never fiered up. at the time i had the center console off and i grounded the black-white wire in the diognostic terminal and then i could hear the fuel pump running and when i tried to start it it fiered up. it runs very rough and only when the terminal is grounded. if the terminal becomes ungrounded it will die even at speed. iv tried the coil, fuel relay, and pcv valve. what can it be???? somebody said it might be the cam sensor or the computer??? please help....im lost||||reg||5
