Z||000008||ray b||10-26-2001||11:20 PM||||OK if the check code donot flash on the dash i bet on a bad computer or wires<BR>when you short it the code should flash<BR>do a search on code and how to flash them.<BR>make sure the codes arenot working if so<BR>you are now in limp mode as car is barely runing thats allso means computer is out.<BR>pick and pull yard for used computer unless you like to over pay dealers or ask in the mall here many of us have old parts around.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000009||StuGood||10-28-2001||05:28 PM||||Please check the ignition timing before you start swapping parts.  Swapping computers is expensive.  Figure out what's wrong before you start swapping parts (unless they're  cheap and easy to replace).<P>It's possible your timing chain skipped a tooth - especially if you shifted down as you approached the intersection.  Result:  way -retarded timing.  Grounding the diagnostic terminal has a <B>big</B> effect on the ignition timing, so maybe that's why it'll run with the terminal grounded.  <P>Just a theory.  But it's worth checking.||||reg||4
Z||000010||samoht||10-28-2001||05:51 PM||||i thought I r4ead in a thread once that a bad oil pressure sending unit could cause this..  the oil pressure senses to low and shut down the fuel pump to prevent flooding, and by crossing the OBD II terminals it sendind B+ to the fuel pump.. as far as it running bad, when you cross the A/B (i think) it is on straight timing.. I would try adjusting your timing with the OBD terminals crossed, then if it still doesnt run when you pull the jumper out, I think there is a way to by pass the Oil pressure sending unit under the hood...  Seems like alot more research is needed.. if it was a chain problem it would not run or run bad all the time.. you may have a compound off problems.. that oil unit has a few funtions.. do a thread search on it and see if some had the same problem..GL<P>85gt3.2<BR>||||reg||1
